 "fill_reason": {
  "pin_bound": "routing/perimeter-bound, not area: 11,914 face pins (W/E 2,554 each, N 3,759, S 3,047); 950.4 x 777.6 keeps every face <= 4 pins/um (N 3,759 / 950.4 = 3.96/um; xgr 734.4 / 648 wide had N 5.1 / 5.8/um) and leaves >= 56 um std-cell bands between every macro column; 37 macros 115.8k + std ~38k um2 -> ~21% fill. Enlarged, never squeezed (PD-AUDIT xg ring)"
 },
 "structural_change": "STW-S81c-COLLA-FRAME (10-22): successor of s81sl_xgr (0397b9edc; standalone native census FAIL max 43: u_c.u_s.g_pb[a].s_q0 / s_q1 one-hot q decodes, 6 drivers 42-43 loads) with PD-AUDIT MUST-DO: (1) master ot_s81sl_xgr3m = ot_s81sl_xgr2 with ot_s81sl_xs6 (per-bank kept q-code copies + kept decode per line pair, <= 16 loads; calendar fetch compares registered as next-state compares: due5 -> fetch one AND-OR, no edge added), same ports / edges; (2) outline 734.4 -> 950.4 wide (N face 3,759 pins <= 4/um), macro columns re-spaced (>= 56 um bands), abutted 0.024-um stack seams + every sub-20-um macro channel hard-blocked (macro_channel_block.tcl at POST_IO_PLACEMENT); (3) k-means K 32 (gate measures pin-flop spread <= 80 per root TT+FF).",
